-- An ASSUME inside a WHERE. There is no section for it to move to, so the
-- warning offers the rule's own GIVEN instead of a section GIVEN, and a
-- WHERE-local type ASSUME is sent to the top of the file, since a WHERE
-- cannot hold a DECLARE. Pinned after the 2026-09-07 refuters showed the
-- section-GIVEN advice hoisting a local binding to module scope
-- (IMPLICIT-PROPS-DESIGN.md §11.1.2).

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `above the threshold` IF n AT LEAST threshold
  WHERE
    ASSUME threshold IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a widget` IS `some widget is present`
  WHERE
    ASSUME Widget IS A TYPE
    ASSUME `some widget is present` IS A BOOLEAN

#CHECK `above the threshold`
#CHECK `has a widget`
